get.description:
Resolves a campaign code (scoped to the store's brand) → `{ id, campaignName, campaignCode }`. Unknown code, store missing, or campaign not available at this store today (API-088 §19.1a: accepting, JST today within recruitment_start..recruitment_end, linked and published to the store) → 404 E-CMP-001.

**OGF code (APP-F-01 FR-M009)** — send `employeeCode` (従業員番号) and `ogfType` (`owner` = 本人, `family` = 家族 within the second degree) with the code. The response is the same; the code is then also checked as the submit will check it, so a pair that passes here is accepted by `POST /api/v1/members/me/enrollment` with the same `employeeCode` / `ogfType` and `promotionCode` = this code:
- only one of the two sent → 400 E-VAL-001 (`details[].field` = the missing one);
- the code is not an OGF code → 400 E-VAL-001 (`details: [{ field: "ogfType", code: "invalid_format" }]`);
- the OGF code is disabled, expired, used up or belongs to another campaign → 404 E-CMP-001;
- `ogfType=owner` and another member already holds this `employeeCode` as 本人 → 400 E-VAL-001 (`details: [{ field: "employeeCode", code: "duplicate" }]`). `family` reuses the employee's number freely.

Without the two keys nothing changes — the shipped app's call (`storeId` + `campaignCode` only) answers as before.
